- op: discuss  # dacd
  at: '2026-06-02T05:47:42Z'  # dacd
  by: agent  # dacd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dacd
  clock: 6  # dacd
  nonce: dacd  # dacd
  message: "Pass-26 provenance-chain probe — INV-lidul status update (partial mitigation observed):\n\nF26.12: `AR.config_fingerprint` is no longer constant across all 84 ARs as INV-lidul's original statement asserts. Pass-26 substrate:\n\n- 30/84 ARs have a unique non-default config_fingerprint\n- 54/84 ARs still have `sha256:44136fa355b3678a` (sha256 of literal `{}` per `_default_config_fingerprint`)\n\nThe 30 populated ARs are: rust, swift, sql, properties, gitignore, requirements, pascal, v, apex, pony, odin, gleam, solidity, janet, fennel, haxe, hack, luau, kdl, smithy, prisma, twig, tcl, sparql, bibtex, bitbake, astro, wgsl, markdown, bash.\n\nThe 54 still-default ARs include exactly WI-mipul's 14-target set (csharp, enclosure-linker, go, html, java, javascript, json, make, manifest_targets, play-routes, python, toml, xml, yaml_ansible) plus 40 linker passes (containment, di-resolution, http-linker, ipc-linker, jackson-dispatch-linker, etc.).\n\nStatus candidate update: INV-lidul is now PARTIALLY MITIGATED. The original \"constant across all 84\" assertion no longer holds at 100%; it holds for 64.3% (54/84). The mitigation appears to be the tree-sitter base-class auto-stamping (which the 30 populated tree-sitter-based analyzers use correctly) plus probably an INV-morag-adjacent producer wiring (since the populated set includes many tree-sitter language-pack passes). WI-mipul's remaining work is the override-analyze() set (14 ARs) and the linker passes that bypass the base class.\n\nPass_version='' on the same 14 ARs (F26.13 elsewhere) confirms WI-mipul's scope. INV-lidul could either:\n1. Move to `pending_validation` with updated statement: \"config_fingerprint is constant for WI-mipul's 14 override-analyze() targets and all linker passes (~54 ARs)\" — would close partly when WI-mipul ships.\n2. Stay `violated` with the original claim acknowledged as quantitatively off; defer the rewrite until WI-mipul ships.\n\nNo new tracker action required at this level; status update is human-decision territory."  # dacd
